From: ThorOS maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] ppp: preserve per-protocol and data-path policy across offload

PPP ioctl policy does not use the netdevice flags/MTU paths. Fence actual
changes with the channel generation and refuse new DIRECT recipes when
PPP must filter, compress, loop or reject the flow. Keep IPv4/IPv6 NPMODE
independent, preserve normal CCP_OPEN negotiation, and do not add a per-
packet path walk. Installed compressors must observe plain packets too.
Both native and compat filter ioctls use the same transactional helper.

